</p>
<p>Suppose I&#8217;m asked first and I answer no. This tells you that I&#8217;m not holding the number 1, because if I were I&#8217;d know for certain that you held 2.</p>
<p>The interlocutor turns to you and asks whether you know my number. You say no. This tells me that you don&#8217;t hold 2, by the same principle &#8212; I know that you just inferred that I&#8217;m not holding 1, so if you held 2 you&#8217;d know that I must have 3.</p>
<p>And so on. Together we&#8217;ll work our way up the number line until one of us says yes.</p>
